tile.betteroplenty.malachite.ore.desc=Bands of malachite embedded in stone.
tile.betteroplenty.malachite.block.desc=A solid block of malachite.
item.betteroplenty.malachite.desc=A banded green stone. Softer-looking than it is.
tile.betteroplenty.sapphire.ore.desc=A chunk of sapphire embedded in stone.
tile.betteroplenty.sapphire.block.desc=A solid block of sapphire.
item.betteroplenty.sapphire.desc=A cold blue gem, harder than it looks.
item.betteroplenty.gem_star.desc=Five gems from five climates, fused into one star. It remembers every place you dug.

# --- Entities (mobs agent) ----------------------------------------------------
# Passed as EntityDispatcher.addMapping's nameKey. A null key is not cosmetic:
# ScreenWorldSettings gates its per-mob spawn toggles on nameKey != null, so an
# unnamed mob cannot be switched off in world settings. See BOPEntities.
entity.betteroplenty.jungle_spider.name=Jungle Spider
entity.betteroplenty.rosester.name=Rosester
entity.betteroplenty.bird.name=Bird
entity.betteroplenty.wasp.name=Wasp
entity.betteroplenty.pixie.name=Pixie
entity.betteroplenty.glob.name=Glob
entity.betteroplenty.phantom.name=Phantom

# Projectiles. A thrown entity is never named on screen, but a null nameKey also
# costs the display name a chunk-load debug view shows. See BOPProjectiles.
entity.betteroplenty.mudball.name=Mudball
entity.betteroplenty.dart.name=Dart

# --- Fluids (fluids agent) ----------------------------------------------------
# Four blocks: BTA models a fluid as a still/flowing pair, so each fluid is two blocks and each
# gets its own name, the way tile.fluid.water.still/flowing do. Neither is in the creative menu --
# you get a fluid from a bucket -- but both still need keys, because /give and the block-picker
# reach them.
tile.betteroplenty.fluid.liquid.poison.still.name=Still Liquid Poison
tile.betteroplenty.fluid.liquid.poison.flowing.name=Flowing Liquid Poison
tile.betteroplenty.fluid.spring.water.still.name=Still Spring Water
tile.betteroplenty.fluid.spring.water.flowing.name=Flowing Spring Water
tile.betteroplenty.fluid.liquid.poison.still.desc=Liquid poison that does not flow when placed. Standing in it sickens you, and no armour will help.
tile.betteroplenty.fluid.liquid.poison.flowing.desc=Liquid poison that flows when placed. It will not eat through stone.
tile.betteroplenty.fluid.spring.water.still.desc=Spring water that does not flow when placed. Bathe in it and your wounds close.
tile.betteroplenty.fluid.spring.water.flowing.desc=Spring water that flows when placed.

# The amethyst bucket. Its contents live in stack NBT on BTA's shared bucket-state axis, so the
# key is the item's own plus the state name with underscores stripped -- ItemBucket.getLanguageKey
# builds it. It carries BTA's five fluids as readily as BOP's two, so all seven need naming.
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.name=Amethyst Bucket
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.desc=Used to hold various liquids. This one takes two loads to an iron bucket's one.
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.springwater.name=Amethyst Bucket of Spring Water
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.springwater.desc=A double bucket full of steaming spring water. Drink it to mend slowly.
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.liquidpoison.name=Amethyst Bucket of Liquid Poison
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.liquidpoison.desc=A double bucket carefully filled with liquid poison. Do not drink it.
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.water.name=Amethyst Water Bucket
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.water.desc=A double bucket full of the deep blue.
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.lava.name=Amethyst Lava Bucket
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.lava.desc=A double bucket full of molten rock. Hot!
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.acid.name=Amethyst Acid Bucket
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.acid.desc=A double bucket carefully filled with vile acid.
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.milk.name=Amethyst Bucket of Milk
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.milk.desc=Doubly good for your bones.
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.icecream.name=Amethyst Bucket of Ice Cream
item.betteroplenty.bucket_amethyst.icecream.desc=A double helping of the frosty treat.

# BTA's own buckets can carry BOP's fluids too -- registering a bucket state is global, so iron and
# steel learn both the moment BOPFluids runs. Their keys are BTA's, defined here because the states
# are ours. BOPFluids.audit() walks every bucket against every state and names anything missing.
item.bucket.iron.springwater.name=Iron Bucket of Spring Water
item.bucket.iron.springwater.desc=A bucket full of steaming spring water. Drink it to mend slowly.
item.bucket.iron.liquidpoison.name=Iron Bucket of Liquid Poison
item.bucket.iron.liquidpoison.desc=A bucket carefully filled with liquid poison. Do not drink it.
item.bucket.steel.springwater.name=Steel Bucket of Spring Water
item.bucket.steel.springwater.desc=A large bucket full of steaming spring water. Drink it to mend slowly.
item.bucket.steel.liquidpoison.name=Steel Bucket of Liquid Poison
item.bucket.steel.liquidpoison.desc=A large bucket carefully filled with liquid poison. Do not drink it.

# --- Ground cover (ground-cover agent) -----------------------------------------------------
# BOP's `foliage` and `plants` metadata blocks, split into standalone blocks, plus the two hanging
# mosses. Names are upstream's own from biomesoplenty.lang -- including the fact that both halves of
# a two-tall plant share the single plant's name, because a player only ever holds one item. Wild
# carrot is the exception: upstream never gives that block a name at all (only its food item, "Wild
# Carrots"), because picking the block yields the food.
#
# Keys are DOT-separated: BlockBuilder turns "poison_ivy" into tile.betteroplenty.poison.ivy and
# keeps the underscored form only as the namespace id. See the note at the top of this file.
tile.betteroplenty.high.grass.name=High Grass
tile.betteroplenty.high.grass.top.name=High Grass
tile.betteroplenty.bush.name=Bush
tile.betteroplenty.sprout.name=Sprout
tile.betteroplenty.poison.ivy.name=Poison Ivy
tile.betteroplenty.berry.bush.name=Berry Bush
tile.betteroplenty.shrub.name=Shrub
tile.betteroplenty.damp.grass.name=Damp Grass
tile.betteroplenty.koru.name=Koru
tile.betteroplenty.clover.patch.name=Clover Patch
tile.betteroplenty.dead.grass.name=Dead Grass
tile.betteroplenty.desert.grass.name=Desert Grass
tile.betteroplenty.desert.sprouts.name=Desert Sprouts
tile.betteroplenty.dune.grass.name=Dune Grass
tile.betteroplenty.thorn.name=Thorns
tile.betteroplenty.barley.name=Barley
tile.betteroplenty.cattail.name=Cattail
tile.betteroplenty.cattail.top.name=Cattail
tile.betteroplenty.cattail.bottom.name=Cattail
tile.betteroplenty.river.cane.name=River Cane
tile.betteroplenty.wild.carrot.name=Wild Carrot
tile.betteroplenty.tiny.cactus.name=Tiny Cactus
tile.betteroplenty.reed.name=Reed
tile.betteroplenty.root.name=Root
tile.betteroplenty.moss.name=Moss
tile.betteroplenty.tree.moss.name=Tree Moss

# Descriptions. Each one says where it grows, because soil is the only thing that distinguishes
# half this family, and names the mechanic where there is one -- the two that hurt, the two that
# come in pairs, and the one that has to stand beside water.
tile.betteroplenty.high.grass.desc=Grass past your knees. Cut the top and the rest goes back to ordinary grass.
tile.betteroplenty.high.grass.top.desc=The upper half of a stand of high grass. It cannot stand without the lower.
tile.betteroplenty.bush.desc=A low, woody tuft. It will grow in the dark where flowers will not.
tile.betteroplenty.sprout.desc=A thin green shoot, barely up yet.
tile.betteroplenty.poison.ivy.desc=Do not wade through it. Leather boots and leggings will save you.
tile.betteroplenty.berry.bush.desc=A bush heavy with fruit. Shears take the bush and leave the berries.
tile.betteroplenty.shrub.desc=A leafy tuft that takes the colour of the trees around it.
tile.betteroplenty.damp.grass.desc=Grass that never quite dries out.
tile.betteroplenty.koru.desc=A tight green spiral, waiting to unfurl.
tile.betteroplenty.clover.patch.desc=Clover pressed flat to the ground. You will walk over it without noticing.
tile.betteroplenty.dead.grass.desc=Brittle and colourless. It wants dry ground and nothing else.
tile.betteroplenty.desert.grass.desc=Tough grass off the red rock. It grows nowhere softer.
tile.betteroplenty.desert.sprouts.desc=Small shoots that have made a go of it somewhere hot.
tile.betteroplenty.dune.grass.desc=Coarse grass that binds sand together. It will only grow on it.
tile.betteroplenty.thorn.desc=Brushing past costs you. Pulling it up costs you twice, unless you use shears.
tile.betteroplenty.barley.desc=A ripe head of grain. Three of them make a wheat.
tile.betteroplenty.cattail.desc=A marsh reed. It only grows on grass with water beside it.
tile.betteroplenty.cattail.top.desc=The head of a tall cattail, standing on its own stem.
tile.betteroplenty.cattail.bottom.desc=The stem of a tall cattail, holding the head up.
tile.betteroplenty.river.cane.desc=A jointed stalk. It grows on grass, and on itself.
tile.betteroplenty.wild.carrot.desc=A white flower with something worth digging up underneath.
tile.betteroplenty.tiny.cactus.desc=Ankle-high and just as sharp as the tall kind.
tile.betteroplenty.reed.desc=It stands in the water rather than beside it.
tile.betteroplenty.root.desc=A root come through a cave roof, hanging in the dark.
tile.betteroplenty.moss.desc=A green sheet on damp stone. Grind it into green dye, or wrap it round cobble.
tile.betteroplenty.tree.moss.desc=Moss hanging out of a canopy. You will need shears to take it.

# Short and medium grass -- the settled canonical grass (atlas 9a E2), landed with the pilot batch.
tile.betteroplenty.short.grass.name=Short Grass
tile.betteroplenty.short.grass.desc=Grass kept low by the wind. Shears will lift it whole.
tile.betteroplenty.medium.grass.name=Medium Grass
tile.betteroplenty.medium.grass.desc=Grass at shin height, between the short stuff and the tall.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BOP's flowers and mushrooms: `flowers` (16), `flowers2` (7 -- lavender is above, with Lavender
# Fields) and `mushrooms` (5). Keys are DOT-separated because HalpLibe rewrites a block's
# underscores; "blue_milk_cap" is tile.betteroplenty.blue.milk.cap, not blue_milk_cap.
#
# Names are upstream's own, from biomesoplenty.lang, including the ones that read oddly next to
# BTA's: BOP's `deadbloom` shows as "Deathbloom", its `rainbowflower` as "Chromaflora", and both
# halves of the sunflower are just "Sunflower". Two land close to a BTA name and both are
# deliberate -- BTA's yellow flower is called Dandelion and BOP's is the White Dandelion (the seed
# head, which is why it grinds to silver), and BTA's light blue flower is a Bluebell where BOP's
# is a cluster of Bluebells that grinds to blue. Each .desc names the dye, which is the only way
# to tell them apart in game.
tile.betteroplenty.clover.name=Clover
tile.betteroplenty.swamp.flower.name=Swampflower
tile.betteroplenty.deathbloom.name=Deathbloom
tile.betteroplenty.glow.flower.name=Glowflower
tile.betteroplenty.hydrangea.name=Blue Hydrangea
tile.betteroplenty.cosmos.name=Orange Cosmos
tile.betteroplenty.daffodil.name=Pink Daffodil
tile.betteroplenty.wildflower.name=Wildflower
tile.betteroplenty.violet.name=Violet
tile.betteroplenty.anemone.name=White Anemone
tile.betteroplenty.lily.flower.name=Waterlily
tile.betteroplenty.rainbow.flower.name=Chromaflora
tile.betteroplenty.bromeliad.name=Bromeliad
tile.betteroplenty.sunflower.name=Sunflower
tile.betteroplenty.sunflower.top.name=Sunflower
tile.betteroplenty.dandelion.name=Dandelion Puff
tile.betteroplenty.hibiscus.name=Pink Hibiscus
tile.betteroplenty.lily.of.the.valley.name=Lily of the Valley
tile.betteroplenty.burning.blossom.name=Burning Blossom
tile.betteroplenty.goldenrod.name=Goldenrod
tile.betteroplenty.bluebells.name=Bluebells
tile.betteroplenty.miners.delight.name=Miner's Delight
tile.betteroplenty.icy.iris.name=Icy Iris
tile.betteroplenty.toadstool.name=Toadstool
tile.betteroplenty.portobello.name=Portobello
tile.betteroplenty.blue.milk.cap.name=Blue Milk Cap
tile.betteroplenty.glowshroom.name=Glowshroom
tile.betteroplenty.flat.mushroom.name=Flat Mushroom

tile.betteroplenty.clover.desc=Three leaves pressed flat to the ground. Lucky, if you find a fourth.
tile.betteroplenty.swamp.flower.desc=A pale bloom off the wet ground. Grind it into cyan dye.
tile.betteroplenty.deathbloom.desc=Do not touch it, and do not pick it bare-handed. Leather boots and leggings will see you past; shears will get you the flower. Grind it into black dye.
tile.betteroplenty.glow.flower.desc=A bloom that gives off its own light. Nobody has found a use for it yet.
tile.betteroplenty.hydrangea.desc=A head of blue florets. Grind it into light blue dye.
tile.betteroplenty.cosmos.desc=A tall orange bloom on a thin stem. Grind it into orange dye.
tile.betteroplenty.daffodil.desc=A pink trumpet, low to the ground. Grind it into pink dye.
tile.betteroplenty.wildflower.desc=It grows wherever it likes. Grind it into magenta dye.
tile.betteroplenty.violet.desc=A small dark bloom that prefers the cold. Grind it into purple dye.
tile.betteroplenty.anemone.desc=White petals round a dark eye. Grind it into white dye.
tile.betteroplenty.lily.flower.desc=A bloom that sits on floating leaves. It needs algae under it to stand.
tile.betteroplenty.rainbow.flower.desc=Its colour will not settle. It grows in the dark as readily as the light.
tile.betteroplenty.bromeliad.desc=A spiny rosette off the hot ground. It grows on sand and nothing softer.
tile.betteroplenty.sunflower.desc=Two blocks tall, and the head is the half worth having. Plant it where there is room above.
tile.betteroplenty.sunflower.top.desc=The head of a sunflower. Break it and the stalk goes with it.
tile.betteroplenty.dandelion.desc=The seed head, gone to white. Grind it into silver dye.
tile.betteroplenty.hibiscus.desc=A wide pink bloom. Grind it into pink dye.
tile.betteroplenty.lily.of.the.valley.desc=Small white bells on a stem. Grind it into white dye.
tile.betteroplenty.burning.blossom.desc=It grows on netherrack and it is still hot. Standing in it sets you alight; shears will get you the flower. Grind it into orange dye.
tile.betteroplenty.goldenrod.desc=A yellow plume. Grind it into yellow dye.
tile.betteroplenty.bluebells.desc=A cluster of deep blue bells. Grind them into blue dye.
tile.betteroplenty.miners.delight.desc=It grows on bare stone deep down, where nothing else does. A good sign you are in the right place.
tile.betteroplenty.icy.iris.desc=A pale iris that only opens in the cold. Grind it into light blue dye.
tile.betteroplenty.toadstool.desc=Red with white flecks. Do not eat it.
tile.betteroplenty.portobello.desc=A broad brown cap. This one you can eat.
tile.betteroplenty.blue.milk.cap.desc=It bleeds blue where you cut it. Grind it into blue dye.
tile.betteroplenty.glowshroom.desc=A cave mushroom that lights its own patch of floor. Grind it into lime dye.
tile.betteroplenty.flat.mushroom.desc=A flat brown cap, almost a plate. Grind it into brown dye.

# ---- The coastline lane: six terrain-placed biomes and BOP's underwater flora ----
# Display names are upstream's setBiomeName(...), not the class names -- BiomeGenBeachGravel shows
# as "Gravel Beach" and BiomeGenOceanAbyss as "Oceanic Abyss".
biome.betteroplenty.bop.shore=Shore
biome.betteroplenty.bop.beach_gravel=Gravel Beach
biome.betteroplenty.bop.beach_overgrown=Overgrown Beach
biome.betteroplenty.bop.ocean_abyss=Oceanic Abyss
biome.betteroplenty.bop.ocean_coral=Coral Reef
biome.betteroplenty.bop.ocean_kelp=Kelp Forest

# The ocean lane: the fourth member of BiomeLayerBiomes' ocean pool, which upstream took from
# vanilla (BiomeGenBase.ocean, setBiomeName("Ocean")). Placed by the land/water mask rather than by
# climate, and it is what the three above are dotted into.
biome.betteroplenty.bop.ocean=Ocean

# Block names follow upstream's tile.bop.coral.* where it has them. The three strand segments have
# no upstream name because getSubBlocks hides them; they still get both keys, because BOPAudit
# walks the registry rather than the creative menu and a hidden block with no name is still a raw
# key in a tooltip the moment anything shows one.
tile.betteroplenty.kelp.bottom.name=Kelp
tile.betteroplenty.kelp.middle.name=Kelp
tile.betteroplenty.kelp.top.name=Kelp
tile.betteroplenty.kelp.name=Kelp
tile.betteroplenty.coral.pink.name=Pink Coral
tile.betteroplenty.coral.orange.name=Orange Coral
tile.betteroplenty.coral.blue.name=Blue Coral
tile.betteroplenty.coral.glow.name=Glowing Coral

tile.betteroplenty.kelp.bottom.desc=The foot of a kelp strand, rooted to the sea bed.
tile.betteroplenty.kelp.middle.desc=A length of kelp, holding up whatever grows above it.
tile.betteroplenty.kelp.top.desc=The tip of a kelp strand. Break what is under it and it goes too.
tile.betteroplenty.kelp.desc=A frond off the sea bed. Plant it underwater on sand, dirt, clay, stone or sponge.
tile.betteroplenty.coral.pink.desc=A reef-builder. It only grows underwater, and it will not stand in the open air.
tile.betteroplenty.coral.orange.desc=Bright enough to spot from the surface on a clear day.
tile.betteroplenty.coral.blue.desc=The colour of the water it grows in, which is no help at all when you are looking for it.
tile.betteroplenty.coral.glow.desc=It lights the sea floor around it. The only lamp down here.

