biome.betteroplenty.bop.arctic=Arctic
biome.betteroplenty.bop.glacier=Glacier
biome.betteroplenty.bop.icy_hills=Icy Hills
biome.betteroplenty.bop.frost_forest=Frost Forest
biome.betteroplenty.bop.coniferous_forest_snow=Snowy Coniferous Forest
biome.betteroplenty.bop.dead_forest_snow=Snowy Dead Forest
biome.betteroplenty.bop.tundra=Tundra
biome.betteroplenty.bop.maple_woods=Maple Woods
biome.betteroplenty.bop.crag=Crag

# Their two surface stones. Block keys are dot-separated, so hard_ice is tile.betteroplenty.hard.ice
# -- writing the underscore localises nothing. Names are upstream's own, from biomesoplenty.lang
# (tile.bop.generic.hard_ice, tile.bop.generic.crag_rock), including the fact that BOP calls the
# block "Hardened Ice" while its field, its texture and its biome all say hard ice.
tile.betteroplenty.hard.ice.name=Hardened Ice
tile.betteroplenty.crag.rock.name=Crag Rock
tile.betteroplenty.hard.ice.desc=Glacier ice, packed until it takes a pickaxe. It will not melt and it will not float.
tile.betteroplenty.crag.rock.desc=The black stone a crag is made of, all the way down. Nothing grows on it.

# ---- Batch 5: the temperate forests, and the Garden's four blocks ----
# Display names are upstream's setBiomeName(...), not the class names -- BiomeGenTimberThin shows
# as "Thinned Timber". "Seasonal Forest" deliberately duplicates BTA's own biome of that name: E5
# drops only biomes/vanilla/, and BOP's Seasonal Forest is a real original biome with its own trees
# (atlas §0's collision table). Nothing in the port keys off the display string.
biome.betteroplenty.bop.cherry_blossom_grove=Cherry Blossom Grove
biome.betteroplenty.bop.deciduous_forest=Deciduous Forest
biome.betteroplenty.bop.garden=Garden
biome.betteroplenty.bop.seasonal_forest=Seasonal Forest
biome.betteroplenty.bop.seasonal_spruce_forest=Seasonal Spruce Forest
biome.betteroplenty.bop.temperate_rainforest=Temperate Rainforest
biome.betteroplenty.bop.timber=Timber
biome.betteroplenty.bop.timber_thin=Thinned Timber

# The Garden's blocks. Upstream names: tile.bop.longGrass, tile.bop.petals.bigflowerred /
# .bigfloweryellow, and the stem has none of its own (BlockBOPLog skips metadata 11 in its texture
# loop, so it never got a name either).
tile.betteroplenty.long.grass.name=Long Grass
tile.betteroplenty.long.grass.desc=Deep, unmown turf. Only the Garden grows it, and only it will hold a giant flower up.
tile.betteroplenty.big.flower.stem.name=Giant Flower Stem
tile.betteroplenty.big.flower.stem.desc=Five blocks of it hold a canopy of petals overhead. Not a tree, whatever it looks like.
tile.betteroplenty.big.flower.red.name=Red Giant Flower
tile.betteroplenty.big.flower.red.desc=Petals the size of a floor. Cut them and one in twenty leaves a rose behind.
tile.betteroplenty.big.flower.yellow.name=Yellow Giant Flower
tile.betteroplenty.big.flower.yellow.desc=Wider and squatter than the red one. One in twenty cuts leaves a dandelion.

