# --- The turnip crop and its seed. Upstream: item.bop.turnipseeds.name=Turnip Seeds; the crop
#     BLOCK has no upstream lang key at all, because 1.6.4 named it off the item form and BOP
#     never gave that one either. The name here is the plain one a player would expect.
#
# WARNING: THE TWO SIDES USE DIFFERENT KEY CONVENTIONS, and only one of them is audited.
#     A BLOCK key turns underscores into DOTS -- turnip_crop -> tile.betteroplenty.turnip.crop
#     (compare tile.betteroplenty.holy.stone.mossy above). An ITEM key KEEPS the underscore
#     -- turnip_seeds -> item.betteroplenty.turnip_seeds (compare item.betteroplenty.wood_scythe).
#     Writing the block key with an underscore is caught at startup by the lang audit;
#     writing the item key with dots is NOT caught by anything and ships an item whose name
#     in the menu is its own raw key.
