# honeycomb, which the hive's filled cells now drop.
achievement.betteroplenty.honey=Bittersweet
achievement.betteroplenty.honey.desc=The land of blood and honey.

# achPromised -- upstream's special-framed arrival in the Promised Land.
achievement.betteroplenty.promised=Movin' On Up!
achievement.betteroplenty.promised.desc=Welcome to the Promised Land!

# The rest of the honey branch, 2026-07-29 -- all three strings verbatim from upstream's
# en_US.lang:440-445. They came off the deferred list when their content turned out to have landed
# in three other lanes; see BOPAchievements' class note.
#
# "A master of disguise" is upstream's joke about the wither wart looking like nether wart, not
# about the Wither -- BOP's wart has nothing to do with that mob and BTA has no Wither at all.
achievement.betteroplenty.wither_wart=Decay
achievement.betteroplenty.wither_wart.desc=A master of disguise.

# "The next Dampe" is upstream's reference to the Zelda gravekeeper; kept verbatim like every other
# string in this file, jokes included.
achievement.betteroplenty.grave=Gravedigger
achievement.betteroplenty.grave.desc=The next Dampe.

achievement.betteroplenty.phantom=Phantom Menace
achievement.betteroplenty.phantom.desc=Stealer of souls...

# achCelestial, upstream's en_US.lang:449-450. Fires on picking up a crystal shard, which the
# Promised Land's crystal blocks drop four of.
achievement.betteroplenty.celestial=Blue Sky
achievement.betteroplenty.celestial.desc=I am the one who...blocks...

# The Promised Land's ground, ids 2200-2205. Upstream packs the four stone variants into one
# metadata block (BlockBOPSkystone) and gives none of them a description, so the names are its
# type strings read out and the descriptions are this port's.
tile.betteroplenty.holy.stone.name=Holy Stone
tile.betteroplenty.holy.stone.desc=The pale bedrock of the Promised Land. Amethyst grows in it, and nowhere else.
tile.betteroplenty.holy.cobble.name=Holy Cobblestone
tile.betteroplenty.holy.cobble.desc=Holy stone, broken and reset.
tile.betteroplenty.holy.bricks.name=Holy Bricks
tile.betteroplenty.holy.bricks.desc=Holy stone cut square. Whoever cut it is long gone.
tile.betteroplenty.holy.stone.mossy.name=Mossy Holy Stone
tile.betteroplenty.holy.stone.mossy.desc=Old holy stone, gone green at the seams.
tile.betteroplenty.holy.grass.name=Holy Grass
tile.betteroplenty.holy.grass.desc=Turf that keeps its colour without a sun to feed it.
tile.betteroplenty.holy.dirt.name=Holy Dirt
tile.betteroplenty.holy.dirt.desc=The soil under the Promised Land. It shifts underfoot like gravel.

# The giant mushroom's trunk, split out of the cap's metadata on 2026-07-28.
tile.betteroplenty.mushroom.stem.name=Giant Mushroom Stem
tile.betteroplenty.mushroom.stem.desc=The pale trunk under a giant mushroom's cap.

# The Promised Land -- dimension 3, and its first biome.
dimension.promised.name=The Promised Land
worldType.betteroplenty.bop.promised=Promised Land
biome.betteroplenty.bop.promised_plains=Majestic Meadow
biome.betteroplenty.bop.promised_forest=Wonderous Woods
biome.betteroplenty.bop.promised_shrub=Sublime Shrubland
biome.betteroplenty.bop.promised_swamp=Blessed Bog
tile.betteroplenty.holy.tall.grass.name=Holy Tall Grass
tile.betteroplenty.holy.tall.grass.desc=Bright turf-grass that needs no sun.
tile.betteroplenty.crystal.name=Crystal
tile.betteroplenty.crystal.desc=A clear growth that hangs from holy stone and lights itself.
tile.betteroplenty.cloud.name=Cloud
tile.betteroplenty.cloud.desc=Solid enough to stand on, if you can reach it.
tile.betteroplenty.portal.promised.name=Promised Land Portal
tile.betteroplenty.portal.promised.desc=A gateway to the Promised Land.

# The Ancient Staff and its three parts. Names are upstream's own
# (`item.bop.ancientStaff.*.name`), which is why the spent one is "Depleted" rather than "Broken"
# even though its texture file is ancientstaffbroken.png.
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff.name=Ancient Staff
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff_handle.name=Ancient Staff Handle
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff_pole.name=Ancient Staff Pole
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff_topper.name=Ancient Staff Topper
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff_depleted.name=Depleted Ancient Staff

item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff.desc=Swing it under open sky and the Promised Land comes to you. Once.
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff_handle.desc=Sapphire and tanzanite set in pale stone.
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff_pole.desc=Peridot and malachite set in pale stone.
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff_topper.desc=Ruby and topaz under a Gem Star.
item.betteroplenty.ancient_staff_depleted.desc=Spent. Another Gem Star would wake it.

# The staff's chat lines. The first two are upstream's `phrase.bop.promisedPortalOverworld` and
# `phrase.bop.promisedPortalOther`, verbatim; the second two are this port's, because upstream
# refuses silently and a one-shot item that appears to do nothing reads as a broken one.
phrase.betteroplenty.promisedPortalOverworld=A gateway to the Promised Land has appeared in the sky above.
phrase.betteroplenty.promisedPortalOther=A gateway to the Overworld has appeared in the sky above.
phrase.betteroplenty.staffWrongDimension=The staff is silent here.
phrase.betteroplenty.staffNoRoom=There is no room in the sky above.
